usage: plot.py [-h] [--input INPUT] --output OUTPUT [--reference]
               [--reference-dir REFERENCE_DIR] [--group GROUP]
               {tables,liegroups,sweep,highd,ablations,embeddings}

Render actual experiment outputs or explicitly labeled historical references.
Examples: python -m paper.plot tables --input runs/results --output
figures/tables python -m paper.plot sweep --reference --output figures/sweep

positional arguments:
  {tables,liegroups,sweep,highd,ablations,embeddings}

optional arguments:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --input INPUT         Results directory, comparison JSON, or explicit plot-
                        data JSON.
  --output OUTPUT       Output directory for PNG, PDF, CSV and provenance
                        JSON.
  --reference           Use labeled archived/paper-reported reference data; no
                        model execution.
  --reference-dir REFERENCE_DIR
  --group GROUP         Optional group/cohort ID selector; repeat for several
                        explicit groups.
